        "answer": {
          "short": "Mean: $\\frac{355}{19}\\approx18.7$ red cards (1 d.p.); median: $18$ red cards; range: $13$ red cards. The mean and range decrease; the median is unchanged.",
          "worked": "Removing $46$ leaves $19$ values.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Remaining total}&=401-46\\\\\\text{Remaining total}&=355\\text{ red cards}\\\\\\text{Mean}&=\\frac{355}{19}\\text{ red cards}\\\\\\text{Mean}&\\approx18.7\\text{ red cards}\\quad\\text{(1 d.p.)}\\end{align*}$$\nThe middle value is now the 10th value, which is $18$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Median}&=18\\text{ red cards}\\\\\\text{Range}&=27-14\\\\\\text{Range}&=13\\text{ red cards}\\end{align*}$$\nThe mean decreases from $20.05$ to approximately $18.7$ red cards. The median stays at $18$ red cards, while the range decreases from $32$ to $13$ red cards.",
